From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tmpfiles: keep /media root:root 0755

webOS OSE's version of this patch ("Change ownership of media directory
to support non-root media services") made /media 0775 media:media, so
that non-root media services could create entries in it. On LuneOS no
media service does: the only entries are /media/internal and
/media/cryptofs, which base-files creates and the Halium initramfs
bind-mounts as root, plus /media/developer, created by root services;
removable storage is mounted under /run/media by udev. With /media
owned by media, mediaindexer - which parses every user file - could
rename /media/internal and leave a symlink in its place for root
services (obexd, umtprd, downloads) to write through.

Make /media 0755 root:root instead. tmpfiles "d" also resets the owner
and mode of an existing /media, so devices that ran the media:media
version are fixed at boot. /media/internal keeps its own 0775
root:media from base-files.

The file keeps its old name so the recipe's SRC_URI does not change.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS/LuneOS specific]
---
 tmpfiles.d/systemd.conf.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tmpfiles.d/systemd.conf.in b/tmpfiles.d/systemd.conf.in
index 6436400cde..e29b4ca50d 100644
--- a/tmpfiles.d/systemd.conf.in
+++ b/tmpfiles.d/systemd.conf.in
@@ -65,3 +65,4 @@ d /var/lib/systemd/ephemeral-trees 0755 root root 0
 d /var/lib/private 0700 root root -
 d /var/log/private 0700 root root -
 d /var/cache/private 0700 root root -
+d /media 0755 root root -
